From 8af23504525b7577ddc74205c7aec03263cc001e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:06:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: say that borg_danger() always rates the full damage on
 purpose

borg_danger() sets its full_damage argument to true before adding up the
danger of each monster, so every caller gets the worst-case estimate
whatever it passes.  The reduced estimate in borg_danger_one_kill() is
still used, but only by callers that invoke it directly.

Add a comment saying the override is deliberate.  Comment only; no code
change.  Nothing becomes dead because of the override: the reduced paths
in borg_danger_one_kill() and borg_danger_physical() stay reachable
through those direct calls.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#69.
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index 11efe9f1a..614f5408d 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -2846,6 +2846,9 @@ int borg_danger(int y, int x, int c, bool average, bool full_damage)
     if (borg.antibounce_count <= 200 && !square_isvault(cave, loc(x, y)))
         p += borg_fear_monsters[y][x] * c;
 
+    /* Grid danger is always the full (worst case) damage, so the
+     * full_damage argument is deliberately overridden.  Reduced estimates
+     * come only from direct calls to borg_danger_one_kill(). */
     full_damage = true;
 
     /* Examine all the monsters */
-- 
